Good short cabling and active termination.
It does cost more, but it helps lots.
If the cables are external buy the thicker "double-wrapped" kind.
Wherever possible use the bigger Centronics50 connectors on external devices
( more contact area, lower resistance). Also gold connectors rather than tinned.

The real problem here, though is that the drivers are just to darned touchy.
Give them any excuse and they will fail. I have devices and cables that,
when running Digital UNIX work just fine on a UDB, but fire up AXP Linux,
and _BLAM_ errors and locked-up machine galore.

