> Adaptec 2940 controller.  It then goes to the autoprobe option, and
> it fails with the complaint:  "I cannot run /bin/insmod: no such file
> or directory", and the whole thing fails miserably.

The problem is that the PC164 kernel from 4.0 doesn't have the AHA2940UW
driver built in, nor available as a module. Try using your 2.0.23 kernel
to do the install, although you may run into a problem if it wasn't built
with the proper ELF support, as all the 4.0 binaries are ELF-format.

> Another thing I don't understand is why the installation
> program does not realize that the scsi driver is already operational
> (milo know about it, and it works properly).

Yes, well, MILO has it builtin, but the kernel doesn't... :-(

> Can anybody  please tell me what I am supposed to do?  All I want is to 
> upgrade from 3.0.3 to 4.0, and get a properly working machine.  Is
> there a way to fix the install images?

I'd say your best bet would be to take 2.0.27, add the axp-diffs-2.0.21 to it,
build a kernel with ELF support and the correct configuration of drivers, and
then use *that* as the kernel you boot to start the install.

Anyone see any problems doing it this way?

--Jay++

